cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Argus, its navigation tooling or its telemetry lab in your own
  work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Argus: a vanilla QuakeC deathmatch bot and telemetry lab"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wall
    given-names: Shane
    alias: saworbit
repository-code: "https://github.com/saworbit/argus"
url: "https://github.com/saworbit/argus"
abstract: >-
  Argus is a deathmatch bot for Quake 1 written in pure vanilla QuakeC, in the
  lineage of the Reaper and Omicron bots. It runs unmodified on any NetQuake
  engine at protocol 15 within a 600-edict ceiling. The repository also holds
  an offline navigation compiler that turns BSP geometry into typed waypoint
  graphs, and a headless lab that compiles, plays and compares botmatches from
  structured telemetry.
keywords:
  - quake
  - quakec
  - game-ai
  - bot
  - goap
  - navigation
license:
  - GPL-2.0-or-later
  - MIT
